            <ObservedData>
              <Attribute Type="Description">In 2 brothers with X-linked myopathy with excessive autophagy (XMEA; 310440) originally reported by Yan et al. (2005), Munteanu et al. (2015) identified a hemizygous c.164-6T-G transversion in intron 2 of the VMA21 gene, resulting in substitution of a purine within a conserved polypyrimidine tract. The mutation was not found in 949 control chromosomes and was not present in public or in-house sequence databases. Patient cells showed decreased VMA21 mRNA (22 to 25% of normal controls) and significantly decreased V-ATPase activity (13% of controls). The patients had a severe congenital form of the disorder, which Munteanu et al. (2015) attributed to the very low V-ATPase activity. The c.164-6T-G mutation is 1 nucleotide from the common XMEA mutation c.164-7T-G (300913.0004).</Attribute>
